.TH SWEETSIDLE 1 "September 2026" "sweetsidle 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sweetsidle \- Wayland idle management daemon for the Sweets compositor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sweetsidle
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B sweetsidle status
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B sweetsidle pause
.br
.B sweetsidle resume
.br
.B sweetsidle reload
.br
.B sweetsidle
.RB [ \-c | \-\-config
.IR PATH ]
.B \-\-check-config
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sweetsidle
is a lightweight Wayland idle daemon for the Sweets compositor.
It uses
.B ext-idle-notify-v1
to run commands when you go idle and when you return.
It also runs hooks for sleep, resume, lock, and unlock, and respects idle
inhibitors by default.
.PP
With no command, it runs in the foreground until stopped.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show daemon, listener, idle-hint, and inhibitor state.
.TP
.B "status --json"
Print the same state as one JSON object with
.BR schema_version ,
.BR paused ,
.BR idle_hint ,
.BR listeners ,
and
.BR inhibitors .
.TP
.B pause
Stop idle timers and clear the idle hint.
Running commands and sleep and lock hooks are not affected.
.TP
.B resume
Restart idle timers from zero.
.TP
.B reload
Queue a config reload; check the logs for the result.
An invalid config keeps the old one active.
Running commands keep running.
Changing a listener that has already timed out rejects the reload; retry after
activity resumes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-c " PATH ", \-\-config " PATH
Read configuration from
.I PATH
instead of the default path.
.TP
.B \-\-check-config
Validate the configuration and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable debug-level runtime logging.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print machine-readable output for the
.B status
command.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print command-line help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The default configuration path is
.IR ~/.config/sweetsidle/config.toml .
The file is UTF-8 TOML, at most 1 MiB, and unknown fields are rejected.
Timeouts are seconds from 1 to 4294967.
Commands must not be empty and run through
.BR "sh -c" .
.PP
The optional
.B [general]
table accepts the following fields:
.TP
.B lock_command
Run on a logind lock request.
.TP
.B unlock_command
Run on a logind unlock request.
Only set this if your locker has a safe unlock command.
.TP
.B before_sleep_command
Run before suspend.
.TP
.B after_resume_command
Run after resume.
.TP
.B wait_before_sleep
Delay suspend until the before-sleep command exits, up to logind's maximum
delay.
Use a locker that daemonizes only after locking.
Defaults to true.
.TP
.B ignore_dbus_inhibit
Ignore
.B org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver
inhibitors.
Defaults to false.
.TP
.B ignore_systemd_inhibit
Ignore systemd-logind idle inhibitors.
Defaults to false.
.PP
The optional
.B [idle_hint]
table has one required
.B timeout
field.
After that many idle seconds, the session is reported idle to logind.
.PP
Each
.B [[listener]]
table accepts:
.TP
.B timeout
Required idle time in seconds.
.TP
.B on_timeout
Run when the timeout expires.
.TP
.B on_resume
Run when activity returns after this timeout.
.TP
.B ignore_inhibit
Run despite all idle inhibitors.
Requires
.B ext_idle_notifier_v1
version 2.
Defaults to false.
.SH EXAMPLE CONFIGURATION
.EX
[general]
lock_command = "sweetslock"
before_sleep_command = "sweetslock --daemonize"
wait_before_sleep = true

[idle_hint]
timeout = 300

[[listener]]
timeout = 300
on_timeout = "sweetslock"
ignore_inhibit = true

[[listener]]
timeout = 600
on_timeout = "sweetsmsg output '*' power off"
on_resume = "sweetsmsg output '*' power on"
.EE
.SH INHIBITORS
Listeners respect compositor, ScreenSaver D-Bus, and systemd-logind
.B idle
inhibitors by default.
The ScreenSaver service answers at
.I /org/freedesktop/ScreenSaver
and
.IR /ScreenSaver .
.B status
lists D-Bus and systemd inhibitors; compositor inhibitors are not visible to
clients.
.SH CONTROL SOCKET
Control commands talk to
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/sweetsidle.sock
(mode 0600).
A live socket prevents a second daemon from starting.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT, SIGTERM
Stop the daemon.
Running commands keep running.
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Same as
.BR reload .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
Used for the default config path.
Must be absolute unless
.B \-\-config
is given.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Holds the control socket.
Required.
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Wayland display to connect to.
.TP
.B XDG_SESSION_ID
Logind session to use.
If unset, the session is looked up by process ID.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sweetsidle/config.toml
Default user configuration.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/sweetsidle.sock
Local control socket.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/sweetsidle.service
Systemd user service.
.TP
.I /usr/share/man/man1/sweetsidle.1
This manual page.
.SH SYSTEMD USER SERVICE
The supplied
.B sweetsidle.service
unit runs with
.BR graphical-session.target .
Enable it with:
.PP
.EX
systemctl --user enable --now sweetsidle.service
.EE
.PP
Don't also start sweetsidle from your compositor config.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B sweetsidle
returns 0 on success and 2 on any error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Validate an explicit configuration:
.PP
.EX
sweetsidle --config ./config.toml --check-config
.EE
.PP
Run with verbose diagnostics:
.PP
.EX
sweetsidle --verbose --config ./config.toml
.EE
.PP
Read the paused state:
.PP
.EX
sweetsidle status --json | jq -r .paused
.EE
.PP
Reload the active configuration:
.PP
.EX
pkill -HUP -x sweetsidle
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd-inhibit (1),
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR loginctl (1)
.PP
